🧩 3. JDK, JRE, JVM (MOST IMPORTANT 🔥)

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

🔹 JVM (Java Virtual Machine)

👉 JVM is responsible for **running Java programs**

✔ Converts bytecode → machine code
✔ Platform dependent

---

🔹 JRE (Java Runtime Environment)

👉 Provides environment to run Java programs

Includes:

* JVM
* Libraries

✔ Required to execute Java code

---

🔹 JDK (Java Development Kit)

👉 Complete package for developers

Includes:

* JRE
* Compiler (javac)
* Tools

✔ Required to develop Java programs

---

📊 Relationship

```text
JDK = JRE + Development Tools
JRE = JVM + Libraries
```

---

🔁 Execution Flow of Java Program

1️⃣ Write code (.java file)
2️⃣ Compile using javac → bytecode (.class)
3️⃣ JVM executes bytecode

---

📌 Flow Diagram (Concept)

```text
.java → Compiler → .class → JVM → Output
```

